      "content": "Thanks, this is much better and feels a lot more professional. \n\nI just ran a quick check on that automated scoring tool we talked about, and it gave this draft a bit of a mediocre score because it feels some of the keywords are a little sparse. I know I told you not to obsess over it, but I'm a bit nervous that if the score is too low, a human won't even see it.\n\nCan you take another pass at it? Try to weave those priority terms—resilience, biodiversity, stewardship, ecosystem, sustainability, mitigation, and restoration—into the text more thoroughly so the score is higher, but try to keep the professional tone we've established. I really want to find that sweet spot where it hits all the marks for the machine without losing the persuasiveness for the actual donors.",
